{"availability":"available","full":"jkdansereau/goldeneye-pc-port","name":"goldeneye-pc-port","description":"GoldenEye 007 (N64, 1997) as a native PC game for Windows, Linux, Steam Deck and macOS. Built from the open decompilation, with widescreen, mouse and keyboard or controller, and split-screen. Not an emulator.","category":"Developer tools","language":"C","stars":270,"forks":27,"created":"2026-08-30T23:02:49Z","updated":"2026-10-14T02:09:45Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://jkdansereau.github.io/goldeneye-pc-port/","topics":["agentic-development","c","claude-code","decompilation","game-porting","goldeneye","goldeneye-007","linux","macos","mips","n64","n64-decomp","nintendo-64","opengl","pc-port","retro-gaming","reverse-engineering","sdl2","steam-deck","windows"],"demo":"https://jkdansereau.github.io/goldeneye-pc-port/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T11:29:53.857Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T11:29:53.857Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T11:29:53.857Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:12.862Z","stars":199,"forks":19},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:43.477Z","stars":213,"forks":22},{"at":"2026-10-12T06:27:54.103Z","stars":229,"forks":22},{"at":"2026-10-18T11:29:53.857Z","stars":270,"forks":27}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["GoldenEye 007 (Nintendo 64, 1997) as a native PC game for Windows, Linux and Steam Deck. Native widescreen, a steady 60 fps, 2–4 player split-screen, mouse and keyboard or a modern controller, rebindable controls and an in-game options menu. No emulator, and not a binary recompilation: the game's own reconstructed C, rebuilt from the GoldenEye 007 decompilation, compiled for your PC and running from your own ROM.","Quick start · Controls · Features · Settings and files · Troubleshooting · Roadmap · Building · Legal","You must supply your own GoldenEye 007 ROM. This repository and its downloads contain no Nintendo code or assets, and no ROM. See What's a ROM? and Legal."],"features":["2–4 player split-screen multiplayer on every MP map, with the N64's own","setup flow and per-player HUD.","Native widescreen at any aspect ratio: the world is undistorted, the HUD","sits at the screen edges, and 4:3 menus are pillarboxed. FOV and draw/LOD distance are adjustable, and AI behaviour stays as on the N64 whatever you set them to.","The original look in one click: the Display mode row (F10 → Video) switches"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jkdansereau/goldeneye-pc-port/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5505a7e77e652ed62e0ec17719d18f578e21a2d388e143d94b434bfd300fc2c5","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:43.607Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:43.607Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"GoldenEye 007 (Nintendo 64, 1997) as a native PC game for Windows, Linux and Steam Deck. Native widescreen, a steady 60 fps, 2–4 player split-screen, mouse and keyboard or a modern controller, rebindable controls and an in-game options menu. No emulator, and not a binary recompilation: the game's own reconstructed C, rebuilt from the GoldenEye 007 decompilation, compiled for your PC and running from your own ROM.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jkdansereau/goldeneye-pc-port/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"5505a7e77e652ed62e0ec17719d18f578e21a2d388e143d94b434bfd300fc2c5","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jkdansereau/goldeneye-pc-port/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:43.608Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T16:07:12Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jkdansereau/goldeneye-pc-port/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:43.610Z","hash":"5505a7e77e652ed62e0ec17719d18f578e21a2d388e143d94b434bfd300fc2c5","originalBytes":38244,"storedBytes":38244,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:43.477Z","subjects":["Games & game development","Apple","MCP servers & agents"],"platforms":["macOS"],"classification"